              '06.1': { type: 'points', points: ['Area 1: correct initial values loaded into R0 and R3: R0 = 0 (0), R3 = 1 (1)', 'Area 2: logical shifting left of register values in loop: R2 = 1100 (12), 11000 (24), 110000 (48); R3 = 10 (2), 100 (4), 1000 (8)', 'Area 3: exiting loop and shifting right: R2 = 11000 (24), R3 = 100 (4)', 'Area 4: first addition and subtraction on R0 and R1: R0 = 100 (4), R1 = 1010 (10)', 'Area 5: addition and subtraction loop: R4 = 0 (0); then R2 = 1100 (12), R3 = 10 (2), R4 = 0 (0); then R2 = 110 (6), R3 = 1 (1); then R4 = 1 (1); then R3 = 0 (0)', 'Area 6: correct final values in registers R0 and R1: R0 = 101 (5), R1 = 100 (4)'], guidance: '6 marks, all AO2. Award marks for the correct values in the indicated areas. Values do not need to be in the exact cells shown, but must be in the correct sequence in the column they are in. Award marks for values written in either decimal or binary; if a binary and a decimal value are written in one cell and one is correct but the other incorrect, treat the cell as correct. Max 5 if any incorrect values in table. Full board trace (R0 | R1 | R2 | R3 | R4): initial R1 = 100010 (34), R2 = 110 (6); R0 = 0, R3 = 1; R2 1100 (12) R3 10 (2); R2 11000 (24) R3 100 (4); R2 110000 (48) R3 1000 (8); R2 11000 (24) R3 100 (4); R0 100 (4) R1 1010 (10) R4 0; R2 1100 (12) R3 10 (2) R4 0; R2 110 (6) R3 1 (1); R0 101 (5) R1 100 (4) R4 1; R3 0.' },
