                  'AO1 — Knowledge': 'Linear search checks each item from the first to the last in sequence. Binary search requires data to be in order... finds the middle value and compares... if the data is less than the middle, repeat with values less... if greater, repeat with values greater. Linear worst-case and average time are linear — grow at the same rate as the number of elements. Binary worst-case and average time are logarithmic — grow logarithmically with the number of elements. Both have the same worst-case space of constant, as the data is not changing during the search.',
