              '11(a)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['Strength: large amount of data collected (1)', 'Strength: method is simple so easy to follow (1) — accept easy to count flowers / easier to count flowers than plants', 'Strength: random sampling, so lack of bias (1)', 'Weakness: area surveyed may not be exactly one m² (1) — accept one m² is a very small / too small an area', 'Weakness: area surveyed may not be chosen randomly (1)', 'Weakness: plants / flowers may be identified incorrectly (1)', 'Weakness: flowers may be counted incorrectly (1)', 'Weakness: we are not told the area surveyed in 2019 (1) — accept area surveyed may be different in the two years', 'Weakness: time of year may vary (1) — accept not all data collected on the same day'], guidance: '5 marks: any five of the nine points. At least one strength and one weakness for full marks. Also accept: not all parts of the UK might be covered.' },
