              '08.5': { type: 'points', points: ['Methanol (is liquid so) can be stored easily or transported easily'], guidance: '1 mark (AO2). More energy can be produced from 1 cm³ of methanol (liquid) than from 1 cm³ of hydrogen (gas) Ignore references to safety and cost Do not accept no greenhouse gas emissions' },
              '09.1': { type: 'points', points: ['Sr(g) + e⁻→ Sr⁺(g) + 2 e⁻'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1). Allow Sr(g) → Sr⁺(g) + e⁻' },
              '09.2': { type: 'points', points: ['M1 V = (d÷t =) 0.950 ÷ 9.47 × 10⁻⁴ OR 1003 m s⁻¹', 'M2 m = 2KE/v² or (2 × 7.02 × 10⁻²⁰)/1003² (= 1.396 x 10⁻²⁵ kg)', 'M3 mass of ion = 1.396 × 10⁻²² (g)', 'M4 mass of one mol of ions in g = 1.396 × 10⁻²² × 6.022 x 10²³ (= 84.04)', 'M5 mass number = 84'], guidance: '5 marks (AO1 ×1; AO2 ×4). Recall and conversion of d into metres. Allow (2 × 7.02 × 10⁻²⁰)/M1² or 2KE t²/d². M3 = M2 x 1000. M4 = M3 x Avogadro’s number; conversion to g may be seen in M4. Answer as whole number.' },
