              '34(a)': { type: 'points', points: ['Concentrations of reactants and products are constant (not equal)', 'Forward and reverse reactions still occurring at the same rate'], guidance: '2 marks (AO3.2 ×2). Also in the mark scheme: To gain both marks there must be some correct reference to a student’s statements.' },
              '34(b)(i)': { type: 'points', points: ['Kc = [CH₃OH] / [CO][H₂]²'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.1).' },
              '34(b)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['[H₂]² = [CH₃OH] / Kc[CO]', '[H₂] =√0.0290 / (4.75 x 10³ x 0.0481)', '[H₂] = 0.0113 mol dm⁻³', '[H₂] = (0.0113 x (9.40 x 10³ / 1000) [H₂] = 0.106 (mol)'], guidance: '4 marks (AO2.6 ×4). Answer line: If answer = 0.106 award 4 marks. ALLOW ecf throughout ALLOW [H₂] =√0.273 / (4.75 x 10³ x 0.452) If MP1, 2 and 3 not scored award 1 mark for correct calculation of concentrations of CO and CH₃OH ALLOW 0.11 if correctly rounded from 0.1059 (not 0.113)' },
              '34(c)*': { type: 'levels', levels: [{ range: [5, 6], descriptor: 'Level 3', criteria: 'Learners give an account of all areas (with some explanatory points) There is a well-developed line of reasoning which is clear and logically structured. The information presented is relevant and substantiated.' }, { range: [3, 4], descriptor: 'Level 2', criteria: 'Learners give an outline account of all areas OR Learners give a detailed account of some areas (with explanatory points from at least two) There is a line of reasoning presented with some structure. The information presented is relevant and supported by some evidence.' }, { range: [1, 2], descriptor: 'Level 1', criteria: 'Learners give an outline account of EITHER yield OR rate for EITHER pressure or temperature There is an attempt at a logical structure with a line of reasoning. The information is in the most part relevant.' }], indicative: { 'Indicative scientific points': 'Pressure - yield; Fewer moles on right/products; High P increases yield of methanol; High P shifts to rhs; (E) poe shifts to side with fewer moles; (E) counteract the change (dec in P) Pressure - rate; High P increases rate of reaction; (E) reacting particles closer together; (E) collide more frequently Temperature - yield; Low T increases yield of methanol; forward reaction is exothermic; Low T shifts to rhs; (E) Low T poe shifts in direction of exo reaction; (E)To counteract the change (increase T); (E) Catalyst has no effect on yield Temperature - rate; Low T decreases rate of reaction; (E) Collisions are less frequent; (E) reacting particles have less energy; (E) fewer collisions have required Ea; (E) Catalyst allows faster rate at lower T AW Conclusions; Temperature is compromise rate/yield; Pressure is a compromise due to cost and safety (AW throughout)' }, guidance: '6 marks (AO2.1 ×3; AO3.2 ×3). Levels of response: OCR\'s marking instructions apply. 0 marks: No response or no response worthy of credit.' },
              '34(d)(i)': { type: 'points', points: ['(∆sysS) positive AND there are more moles/molecules of (gaseous) products than reactants'], guidance: '1 mark (AO2.1).' },
              '34(d)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['∆sysS = Sproducts – Sreactants ∆sysS = [(197.6) + 3(130.7)] – [(186.2) + (188.7)] ∆sysS = [589.4] – [374.9] ∆sysS = 214.8 J K⁻¹ mol⁻¹', '∆totalS =0 = ∆sysS -∆H/T', 'T = ∆H / ∆sysS T = (206 x 1000) / 214.8', 'T = 959 K'], guidance: '4 marks (AO2.2 ×4). Answer line: If answer = 959 K award 4 marks. ALLOW 2 or more sf ALLOW ecf throughout ∆totalS = ∆sysS +(-∆H/T), ∆totalS =0 Final temperature must be positive and correctly rounded to score MP4' },
              '35(a)': { type: 'points', points: ['pharmacophore'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.1).' },
              '35(b)': { type: 'points', points: ['for one solid wedge and one dashed wedge/line'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.1). or one straight line (not at 180 to bond shown) and a dashed line or a wedge. IGNORE the rest of the molecule Bond angles, if shown, must be correct' },
              '35(c)(i)': { type: 'points', points: ['The aluminium(III) chloride reacts (vigorously) with water'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.2).' },
              '35(c)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['electrophilic substitution'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.1).' },
              '35(d)': { type: 'points', points: ['Reactant: CH₃CH₂OH', 'Product: H₂O'], guidance: '2 marks (AO2.5 ×2).' },
              '35(e)(i)': { type: 'points', points: ['Acidified (potassium) dichromate(VI) AND (heat under) reflux'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.2). ALLOW Cr₂O₇²⁻/H⁺' },
              '35(e)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['Warm with Fehling’s solution', '(solution) turns (from blue) orange/red precipitate', 'OR Warm with Tollens’ reagent/ammoniacal silver nitrate', '(solution) turns from colourless to silver ‘mirror’'], guidance: '2 marks (AO1.2 ×2). ALLOW Benedict’s (solution) in place of Fehling’s ALLOW warm with Cr₂O₇²⁻/H⁺ ✓ (orange) to green ✓ Second mark depends on the correct reagent' },
              '35(e)(iii)': { type: 'points', points: ['both ‘curly arrows’ in step 1: from C=O bond to O, and from lone pair of :CN⁻ to Cδ⁺ of C₆H₅CHO [drawn]', 'partial charges and all full –/+ charges', '‘curly arrow’ in step 2: from O⁻ to H⁺, giving C₆H₅CH(OH)CN [drawn]'], guidance: '3 marks (AO1.2 ×3). ALLOW step 2 to follow on from step 1 rather than being written separately Curly arrows must start at a lone pair or – charge or the middle of a bond If the structure of the rest of the molecule is incorrect, ALLOW ecf on subsequent marks ALLOW for step 2' },
              '35(e)(iv)': { type: 'points', points: ['H₂SO₄ + HNO₃ → HSO₄⁻ + NO₂⁺ + H₂O OR 2H₂SO₄ + HNO₃ → 2HSO₄⁻ + NO₂⁺ + H₃O⁺'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.2).' },
              '35(e)(v)': { type: 'points', points: ['to prevent loss of reactants/products/mixture AW'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1.2).' },
